## Path:	Network/Chrony
## Description:	Chrony time synchronization settings
## Type:	string
## Default:	"-s"
## ServiceRestart: chronyd
#
# Command line options for chronyd.
#
# -s sets the clock at start-up from the RTC, or on machines without a
# working RTC forward to the driftfile's timestamp (only if that is later
# than the current and RTC time, i.e. a monotonic last-known-good seed).
# This gives DNSSEC validation, TLS/NTS-KE certificate checks and other
# time-sensitive services a roughly correct clock before the network is
# up, without blocking boot the way waiting for real synchronization does.
#
OPTIONS="-s"
